  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study is a pilot fieldwork project, meaning the findings are highly localized to a single neighborhood and may not represent a fully scaled sensory inventory.",
      "what": "This pilot fieldwork maps the multisensorial characteristics of the Tamburi neighborhood in Taranto, Italy, a district adjacent to a major steel plant undergoing a post-industrial transition. The researchers combined serial visions, soundwalks, and smellscape notation to document the area's sensory landscape, identifying a distinct dissonance between a quiet post-industrial acoustic environment and a dominant industrial visual presence.",
      "why": "It demonstrates how combining visual, auditory, and olfactory mapping can capture the complex, suspended identity of neighborhoods transitioning away from heavy industry, offering a methodology to document urban change beyond standard spatial metrics."
    }
